llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: GVN's scalar PRE reports only its last instruction's change (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION where partial redundancy elimination in
GVN would run a further round. r253518 (llvm-project adb4057a153a,
2015-11-18, first release LLVM 3.8) made GVN::performPRE accumulate
(`Changed |= performScalarPRE(...)`) where earlier releases assigned
(`Changed = ...`), so that a pass over a block that changed only an earlier
instruction started no further round. 0x307330 and 0x402110 keep an
address materialised (`add rax, 0x40`) that the further round folds into
the store; they are equal to the base under the prebuilt 3.7.1 only (round
208B). No source form reaches the number of rounds. With the assignment
restored those two functions compile to the base's bytes and are the only
two of the module's 4,998 that change; no matched game row changes (round
208B's sweep, repeated by the supervisor with this unconditional form).

diff -ru a/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp b/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp
--- a/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp
@@ -2541,7 +2541,9 @@
                               BE = CurrentBlock->end();
          BI != BE;) {
       Instruction *CurInst = &*BI++;
-      Changed |= performScalarPRE(CurInst);
+      // PS4: performPRE reports only the last instruction's PRE, as before r253518 (not taken):
+      // a round that changed only earlier instructions starts no further round.
+      Changed = performScalarPRE(CurInst);
     }
   }
 
